  "sourceReview": [
    "Interface nil/equality and method sets from tagged spec; runtime2 and getitab distinguish two-word representation from language semantics and common lookup from locked insertion.",
    "Defer semantics do not imply a particular return register, stack location or open-coded implementation. Compiler walk/SSA include multiple eligibility conditions. panicnil compatibility also depends on effective GODEBUG/main language version.",
    "API manifests: unique/iter 1.23; weak/AddCleanup 1.24; stable synctest, FlightRecorder, SetDefaultGOMAXPROCS 1.25.",
    "Important actual version difference: AddCleanup 1.26.1 adds direct closure capture and interior-pointer argument guards absent in 1.25.0. These are not arbitrary reachability-graph validation. Both rejection cases executed in a new test.",
    "Weak Value has no eventual-nil guarantee; cleanup timing/order and tiny objects constrain guarantees. Cleanup.Stop needs target reachability across the call for guaranteed removal.",
    "iter.Pull early stop, repeated stop, post-stop next and panic propagation from iter.go; coro is internal optimization, not a permanent thread-affinity/25ns guarantee.",
    "GOMAXPROCS: quotas versus requests, affinity, rounding/minimum, manual overrides, effective GODEBUG compatibility. Relevant debug.go contracts unchanged between checked 1.25/1.26.",
    "synctest: Mutex/RWMutex, I/O and syscalls are not durably blocking. 1.26 docs add self-contained-test guidance; fake-time contract is not zero-flakiness proof.",
    "FlightRecorder MinAge/MaxBytes are not exact duration/memory/snapshot guarantees; Start/WriteTo errors and lifecycle executed with a real recorder and a failing writer."
  ],
